From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cmd: a batch file is read in the console's code page

Windows' cmd reads a batch file's lines in the console's current code
page; Wine's always used the OEM code page, so after "chcp 65001" a UTF-8
script's box drawing and symbols came out as mojibake (David 2026-10-01:
the console looked off). Without a console, the OEM code page as before.

Gate: test/batchcp-gate.sh (mutant SG_MUTANT_BATCH_OEMCP fails it).
---
--- a/programs/cmd/batch.c
+++ b/programs/cmd/batch.c
@@ -242,7 +242,14 @@
       UINT cp;
       const char *p;
 
+      /* Stained Glass OS: as Windows' cmd, a batch file's lines in the
+       * console's code page -- after "chcp 65001" a UTF-8 script's text
+       * (box drawing, symbols) was read as the OEM code page, mojibake */
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_BATCH_OEMCP
       cp = GetOEMCP();
+#else
+      if (!(cp = GetConsoleOutputCP())) cp = GetOEMCP();
+#endif
       bufA = xalloc(noChars);
 
       /* Save current file position */
